WEBVTT

00:11.010 --> 00:13.179
‎GRADE 2 CLASS 2

00:14.014 --> 00:15.682
‎Whoa... Whoa...

00:15.765 --> 00:17.100
‎What a turn of events!

00:17.183 --> 00:18.393
‎IN SUSPENSE
‎BA-BUMP BA-BUMP

00:18.476 --> 00:21.354
‎How on earth did they adapt
‎this narrative trick for the screen?

00:22.188 --> 00:25.191
‎There's another movie based on a book
‎by the same author airing on TV this week.

00:25.275 --> 00:28.570
‎I remember seeing that movie
‎when I was in middle school.

00:29.487 --> 00:30.488
‎With Igarashi.

00:31.030 --> 00:32.824
‎What a good movie.

00:33.324 --> 00:36.286
‎I got lost, like,
‎halfway through that movie.

00:37.996 --> 00:41.708
‎Wait... I may have found it entertaining,

00:43.001 --> 00:44.961
‎but what do other people think?

00:45.962 --> 00:47.213
‎Now what?

00:47.297 --> 00:50.133
‎I really want Amamiya
‎to read the original.

00:50.216 --> 00:51.968
‎Full of oneself.

00:53.720 --> 00:54.721
‎POKE OUT

00:56.598 --> 00:57.599
‎Amamiya.

00:57.682 --> 01:00.226
‎You scared me. What is it?

01:00.894 --> 01:02.187
‎Well...

01:04.564 --> 01:06.649
‎That movie we were
‎talking about this morning...

01:06.733 --> 01:10.695
‎I have the book, so...

01:11.821 --> 01:14.657
‎Would you like to read it?

01:15.825 --> 01:17.160
‎MUTTER MUTTER
‎MUMBLE MUMBLE

01:17.243 --> 01:20.080
‎I mean, if you're gonna watch the movie,
‎then you'd know what it'll be about.

01:20.163 --> 01:22.373
‎But it's kind of thick,
‎so I won't force you to read it--

01:22.457 --> 01:24.501
‎I'll read it. I want to read it.

01:28.254 --> 01:29.547
‎Wow...

01:30.757 --> 01:32.634
‎You have no idea how happy I am.

01:36.930 --> 01:38.264
‎What?

01:38.348 --> 01:39.599
‎Thank goodness!

01:39.682 --> 01:41.684
‎RELIEVED
‎GLAD HE'S INTERESTED IN THE BOOK

01:41.768 --> 01:43.770
‎FLUFFY
‎GLAD SHE REMEMBERED THEIR CONVERSATION

01:44.354 --> 01:45.396
‎Thank you.

01:47.524 --> 01:50.360
‎I didn't see him
‎as this sort of person at first.

01:50.860 --> 01:52.362
‎But now...

01:54.614 --> 01:55.615
‎TEEHEE

01:55.698 --> 01:56.783
‎He's cute.

01:57.325 --> 01:58.535
‎What are you doing?

02:10.130 --> 02:11.756
‎STRETCH - SWISH

02:11.840 --> 02:15.552
‎I really hyped that book up to him.
‎Hopefully he doesn't feel obligated.

02:16.136 --> 02:17.887
‎I'll read it. I want to read it.

02:17.971 --> 02:21.391
‎You have no idea how happy I am.

02:38.867 --> 02:39.909
‎Morning.

02:39.993 --> 02:41.411
‎Morning.

02:41.995 --> 02:43.580
‎You're leaving already?

02:43.663 --> 02:45.999
‎Yeah. I'm preparing a meeting today.

02:47.000 --> 02:48.084
‎All right.

02:48.168 --> 02:50.712
‎There's money next to the whiteboard.

02:50.795 --> 02:51.880
‎Thanks.

02:51.963 --> 02:53.172
‎Make sure you lock up.

02:53.256 --> 02:54.424
‎See you.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.175
‎Take care.

03:03.266 --> 03:05.894
‎Mom always leaves for work early.

03:06.769 --> 03:07.937
‎MONEY FOR FOOD

03:08.021 --> 03:11.399
‎And ever since the divorce,
‎she gets home later and later.

03:13.026 --> 03:15.820
‎I'm usually on my own at home.

03:18.907 --> 03:21.200
‎Sometimes I wonder.

03:21.743 --> 03:23.912
‎Do I even exist?

03:24.621 --> 03:25.622
‎Don't be silly.

03:25.705 --> 03:27.916
‎It can't be helped in my case.

03:28.499 --> 03:29.667
‎Yeah.

03:32.754 --> 03:35.840
‎This is just normal for me.

05:07.557 --> 05:11.978
‎EPISODE 12
‎THUNDER

05:12.854 --> 05:15.356
‎Wow, really?

05:15.440 --> 05:18.109
‎How did you decide on your job?

05:18.192 --> 05:21.738
‎I can never find any good ones
‎in those free newspapers.

05:21.821 --> 05:23.114
‎Well...

05:23.197 --> 05:25.992
‎-I've even registered on an app.
‎-‎So conversational.

05:26.075 --> 05:28.328
‎Why? Why now?

05:29.203 --> 05:30.204
‎SQUEEZE SQUEEZE

05:30.288 --> 05:33.499
‎No. Stop that. It's rude.
‎You're doing it again.

05:33.583 --> 05:36.252
‎STARE

05:39.088 --> 05:40.757
‎SMILE

05:42.717 --> 05:44.218
‎What an aesthetic face...

05:45.595 --> 05:49.140
‎Koyun seems to be getting along well
‎with the first years out of nowhere.

05:49.724 --> 05:50.975
‎How strange.

05:51.059 --> 05:52.894
‎Yeah. When did that happen?

05:52.977 --> 05:54.145
‎How strange.

05:55.354 --> 05:57.398
‎And she's super pretty too!

05:57.482 --> 05:58.649
‎What is she?

06:01.652 --> 06:03.071
‎Well, I didn't see that coming.

06:03.738 --> 06:05.490
‎Okay! Break's over.

06:05.573 --> 06:07.241
‎First years! Could you come here, please?

06:07.325 --> 06:08.659
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

06:09.285 --> 06:12.330
‎The third years are calling.
‎I'd better go.

06:12.413 --> 06:13.414
‎Okay.

06:13.498 --> 06:16.667
‎WAVE WAVE

06:23.508 --> 06:25.676
‎TAP TAP TAP
‎THUMP THUMP - WHACK

06:25.760 --> 06:27.178
‎So it's...

06:33.726 --> 06:35.978
‎Stop that, Hayato...

06:42.401 --> 06:43.402
‎CLENCH

06:43.486 --> 06:44.487
‎Scared you, didn't I?

06:44.570 --> 06:46.322
‎THIS IS PAYBACK FOR THE OTHER DAY
‎SUPER SURPRISED

06:46.405 --> 06:47.448
‎Yeah...

06:47.532 --> 06:50.159
‎I lost Miki and Tsukiko.

06:50.243 --> 06:52.328
‎She's just sitting down.

06:56.415 --> 06:57.834
‎-Minato.
‎-'Aye!

06:58.626 --> 07:00.002
‎"'Aye"?

07:00.086 --> 07:02.088
‎So, this Sunday's tournament,

07:02.171 --> 07:05.091
‎we're short on controllers,
‎so can you bring yours from home?

07:05.174 --> 07:06.801
‎-Yeah, sure.
‎-‎Video games?

07:06.884 --> 07:08.803
‎-How many are coming?
‎-Three.

07:08.886 --> 07:12.306
‎Can you imagine if we had a racing wheel?
‎That'd be the best.

07:12.390 --> 07:14.016
‎Go and buy one, Hayato.

07:14.100 --> 07:15.435
‎I'm paying for it now?

07:17.728 --> 07:19.105
‎FWUMP

07:19.188 --> 07:20.481
‎DEJA VU

07:20.565 --> 07:23.901
‎Come on. I'm clearly in the way here.

07:24.402 --> 07:26.487
‎Sorry about that.

07:27.238 --> 07:30.283
‎I don't care if you're not needed here,
‎or if you think you're in the way.

07:33.202 --> 07:35.580
‎I just want you here with me.

07:38.332 --> 07:39.834
‎I mean, that's it, really...

07:40.918 --> 07:41.919
‎I...

07:49.677 --> 07:50.761
‎What now...

07:50.845 --> 07:51.846
‎SWOOSH

07:51.929 --> 07:55.224
‎The blond one is Daichi Midorikawa.
‎And the other one is in another class.

07:55.308 --> 07:56.309
‎Introduce me properly!

07:56.392 --> 07:57.393
‎HAHAHA

07:57.477 --> 08:00.897
‎It's Haya-to Aka-hoshi!

08:00.980 --> 08:02.273
‎I know, I know.

08:02.356 --> 08:05.776
‎That's "Aka" from "Akahoshi."
‎"Hoshi" from "Akahoshi." It's "Akahoshi"!

08:05.860 --> 08:07.487
‎You need to calm down.

08:08.988 --> 08:11.407
‎201 - HIKAWA
‎401 - AZUMI

08:11.491 --> 08:12.700
‎MIKI'S HOUSE

08:12.783 --> 08:15.703
‎You're really not coming riding
‎with us tomorrow, Koyun?

08:15.786 --> 08:18.498
‎I'm fine.
‎Plus, I've got work in the evening.

08:18.581 --> 08:19.665
‎I see.

08:20.291 --> 08:22.752
‎Let's be real here.
‎I'd definitely be a third wheel.

08:23.753 --> 08:26.672
‎They'd be so cute together!
‎I wish I could see it!

08:27.256 --> 08:28.883
‎TCH...

08:34.388 --> 08:36.933
‎Yota's pretty cool, isn't he?

08:38.351 --> 08:39.936
‎What?

08:40.019 --> 08:42.230
‎He's dependable, and he's always so calm.

08:42.313 --> 08:43.523
‎IT'S THAT WAY

08:43.606 --> 08:44.857
‎Is he?

08:44.941 --> 08:45.942
‎THUNK

08:46.025 --> 08:52.240
‎I really wish I could be
‎as warm and kind as he is.

08:52.323 --> 08:55.243
‎What? So what you're saying is...

08:56.077 --> 08:58.955
‎Koyun. Are Yota and Minato...
‎"different" for you?

08:59.789 --> 09:01.791
‎What? What do you mean by "different"?

09:01.874 --> 09:03.501
‎Why's she bringing up Amamiya?

09:04.085 --> 09:07.255
‎I mean, yeah, of course.
‎They're two different people, so...

09:07.964 --> 09:09.924
‎But that's not what you meant?

09:10.466 --> 09:13.010
‎What's this?
‎She's getting super flustered.

09:14.387 --> 09:18.057
‎I still get kind of nervous
‎when I'm around Amamiya.

09:18.140 --> 09:20.017
‎Sometimes.

09:20.685 --> 09:23.271
‎So she's not nervous around Yota?

09:23.354 --> 09:24.355
‎MUTTER MUTTER

09:24.438 --> 09:28.150
‎I still don't know Amamiya
‎as well as I know Yota, so...

09:28.234 --> 09:32.613
‎But, like, I would like
‎to get to know him better, so...

09:33.155 --> 09:38.327
‎She prides herself on knowing Yota well!

09:46.669 --> 09:48.963
‎Dam!

09:51.173 --> 09:52.925
‎This is so cool!

09:53.926 --> 09:54.927
‎It is pretty neat.

09:55.011 --> 09:58.306
‎It's so neat! My heart's skipping beats!

09:59.932 --> 10:02.351
‎Here, Yota. Get in the photo.

10:06.063 --> 10:08.107
‎Wait, how to fix this?

10:08.190 --> 10:10.318
‎I can't get any of the background.

10:11.193 --> 10:12.403
‎CAN'T THINK OF THE WORD "ARM"

10:12.486 --> 10:15.197
‎You take it, Yota. With your "long limbs."

10:15.281 --> 10:16.616
‎"Long limbs"?

10:17.283 --> 10:18.284
‎Like this?

10:18.367 --> 10:20.369
‎Yeah, just like that! Yay!

10:30.713 --> 10:31.881
‎HAHA

10:47.563 --> 10:49.899
‎That was so much fun.

10:50.483 --> 10:51.484
‎It was.

10:52.151 --> 10:53.152
‎Yota.

10:53.736 --> 10:55.237
‎Where to next?

10:56.614 --> 11:00.034
‎You said you wanted to visit
‎a valley before, right?

11:00.117 --> 11:02.119
‎Shall we go in the summer?

11:05.998 --> 11:08.376
‎We... We could do
‎an abandoned railway track?

11:08.459 --> 11:09.460
‎PLONK

11:09.543 --> 11:10.753
‎Sounds rad!

11:11.754 --> 11:12.755
‎-B!
‎-WB!

11:12.838 --> 11:14.173
‎TRANSLATION: I'M BACK
‎TRANSLATION: WELCOME BACK

11:14.840 --> 11:17.093
‎-How was your date?
‎-Date? You're too funny.

11:17.176 --> 11:18.177
‎AB ROLLER

11:18.260 --> 11:21.013
‎It's not like that with Yota.

11:21.097 --> 11:23.099
‎It's not "man and woman" between us.

11:23.182 --> 11:25.976
‎Man, today was so much fun!

11:26.060 --> 11:27.186
‎Good for you.

11:27.269 --> 11:31.774
‎I mean, yeah, I'd like to have
‎some romance eventually, but...

11:31.857 --> 11:33.359
‎But Yota's different.

11:33.442 --> 11:36.195
‎We're not like that.
‎I could never date him.

11:36.779 --> 11:37.863
‎Really?

11:37.947 --> 11:38.948
‎Yep!

11:39.031 --> 11:42.451
‎Besides, friends come first!

11:44.078 --> 11:45.121
‎You are so right.

11:45.204 --> 11:46.205
‎You see?

11:46.789 --> 11:48.374
‎-Major mood!
‎-Major mood!

11:48.457 --> 11:51.502
‎-Bros before hoes! Chicks before dicks!
‎-Bros before hoes! Chicks before dicks!

11:51.585 --> 11:53.129
‎You got it, my bro!

11:53.212 --> 11:54.797
‎-Damn straight!
‎-Damn straight!

11:54.880 --> 11:56.340
‎-Darn tootin'!
‎-Darn tootin'!

11:56.424 --> 11:57.716
‎-Preach it!
‎-Preach it!

12:09.895 --> 12:13.691
‎Hey, did you get your freebie tickets for
‎that crepe store near the train station?

12:13.774 --> 12:15.484
‎Freebie tickets?

12:15.568 --> 12:17.695
‎Here. I'll send you the URL.

12:17.778 --> 12:20.030
‎You get up to two per person.
‎Make sure you get them.

12:20.114 --> 12:21.365
‎Thanks.

12:25.578 --> 12:28.998
‎MARU: URL FOR THE CREPES

12:34.420 --> 12:38.257
‎You're not gonna take a photo?

12:40.342 --> 12:42.720
‎Right. I guess it is pretty unique.

12:42.803 --> 12:43.804
‎BETTER TAKE A PICTURE

12:43.888 --> 12:45.389
‎It looks unique?

12:46.098 --> 12:48.017
‎I don't know what's come over me.

12:49.226 --> 12:52.563
‎Somehow, Momoka roped me
‎into a little detour on the way home.

12:53.063 --> 12:56.192
‎I'll send you the pic,
‎so can you give me your details?

12:57.151 --> 12:58.235
‎Okay.

12:59.069 --> 13:02.948
‎Koyun. I've got tickets for two free
‎crepes. Want to have my second crepe?

13:03.032 --> 13:04.617
‎Sure.

13:05.451 --> 13:07.536
‎Are you sure you want me?

13:08.078 --> 13:13.918
‎Say, Koyun. You're good friends with guys.
‎How can I be better friends with guys too?

13:14.001 --> 13:15.085
‎What?

13:15.628 --> 13:17.505
‎You're asking me?

13:17.588 --> 13:22.510
‎I really think you're much better
‎at socializing than I am, Momoka.

13:23.093 --> 13:25.137
‎That may be so.

13:25.221 --> 13:26.972
‎She doesn't deny it?

13:27.056 --> 13:31.769
‎But I've never really had
‎a proper friendship with a guy before.

13:32.770 --> 13:35.189
‎I think you'd be popular with the guys.

13:35.272 --> 13:36.440
‎I am.

13:38.609 --> 13:40.945
‎Are you thinking, "She doesn't deny it"?

13:41.028 --> 13:42.029
‎EEK

13:43.697 --> 13:45.699
‎You're so cute, Koyun.

13:46.200 --> 13:49.787
‎I don't think her "cute"
‎is meant to be a compliment.

13:50.371 --> 13:54.792
‎Though, I guess you could be
‎good friends with someone,

13:54.875 --> 13:57.211
‎but then all of a sudden
‎you've caught feels.

13:57.294 --> 13:59.046
‎Has that ever happened with you?

13:59.129 --> 14:00.130
‎What?

14:01.257 --> 14:03.551
‎I don't think so.

14:04.134 --> 14:07.137
‎Really? So you keep everything separate?

14:07.221 --> 14:10.307
‎Why did that stop my thoughts
‎in their tracks for a second?

14:12.393 --> 14:14.395
‎I don't think I could do it.

14:15.396 --> 14:20.109
‎I'd definitely fall in love with Amamiya.

14:21.318 --> 14:25.990
‎A guy as good-looking as him near me?
‎I'd definitely end up head over heels.

14:27.032 --> 14:28.367
‎Good-looking?

14:29.118 --> 14:30.661
‎You think so?

14:31.996 --> 14:35.499
‎I'm very free with my compliments
‎when it comes to Yota...

14:38.335 --> 14:40.796
‎So why do I struggle for words
‎when it comes to Amamiya?

14:41.630 --> 14:43.549
‎GRADE 2 CLASS 2

14:43.632 --> 14:46.051
‎Koyun. Thanks for the book.

14:46.719 --> 14:48.387
‎You finished already?

14:48.470 --> 14:50.848
‎Yeah. I couldn't put it down.

14:50.931 --> 14:53.058
‎And I couldn't wait
‎to talk with you about it.

14:53.726 --> 14:55.436
‎Yeah? I'm glad to hear it.

14:58.147 --> 15:01.191
‎Amamiya... Your feels are showing.

15:01.275 --> 15:03.277
‎Please keep your feels in check.

15:03.944 --> 15:07.865
‎That mood shift in the final chapter
‎really gave me the chills.

15:07.948 --> 15:09.408
‎Me too. I really lik--

15:13.537 --> 15:14.914
‎WHOA

15:15.748 --> 15:20.502
‎A guy as good-looking as him near me?
‎I'd definitely end up head over heels.

15:20.586 --> 15:23.505
‎No, it's not that he's good-looking.

15:23.589 --> 15:25.507
‎It's the things he says.

15:25.591 --> 15:27.468
‎It's the way he acts, and his face.

15:27.551 --> 15:28.886
‎He makes me happy.

15:28.969 --> 15:31.388
‎He gives me butterflies...

15:32.014 --> 15:33.515
‎What's this?

15:34.934 --> 15:36.018
‎What happened?

15:37.394 --> 15:39.855
‎She won't look me in the eye today.

15:40.981 --> 15:43.943
‎Koyuki seems pretty put off.

15:44.443 --> 15:45.653
‎Is she okay?

15:46.236 --> 15:47.571
‎What book is that?

15:47.655 --> 15:48.656
‎BA-BUMP

15:49.281 --> 15:52.660
‎I'd lent it to Amamiya,
‎and he was just giving it back to me.

15:52.743 --> 15:53.911
‎Wanna read it too?

15:53.994 --> 15:54.995
‎SHOCK

15:55.079 --> 15:56.163
‎What?

15:56.956 --> 15:58.540
‎I read it in just two days.

15:59.416 --> 16:01.335
‎It's not a competition, man.

16:09.718 --> 16:10.803
‎What?

16:10.886 --> 16:11.887
‎FIDGET FIDGET

16:11.971 --> 16:16.016
‎Could this be a one-sided thing
‎from Amamiya's side?

16:16.100 --> 16:19.144
‎We use "is not" instead of "does not"
‎in a negative sentence

16:19.228 --> 16:21.063
‎because the subject
‎is third-person singular...

16:21.146 --> 16:23.565
‎What is this feeling?

16:24.274 --> 16:29.822
‎Come on. I'm not so dense
‎as to not know what it really is.

16:30.531 --> 16:33.325
‎What do I do?

16:34.243 --> 16:37.538
‎I've noticed a change in my feelings.

16:38.747 --> 16:39.748
‎But...

16:39.832 --> 16:40.833
‎Koyun! Good morning.

16:40.916 --> 16:42.167
‎WHOOSH

16:42.251 --> 16:43.836
‎In saying that,

16:45.170 --> 16:46.922
‎I don't act on it.

16:48.674 --> 16:50.592
‎I haven't actually changed.

16:56.098 --> 16:58.100
‎I'm just living my life as normal.

17:01.812 --> 17:05.607
‎But this giddy, butterfly kind of state

17:06.942 --> 17:08.402
‎is kind of fun.

17:10.112 --> 17:11.655
‎Then I'll see you tomorrow.

17:11.739 --> 17:13.115
‎-See you!
‎-See you!

17:14.575 --> 17:15.576
‎APPEARS

17:15.659 --> 17:17.661
‎Wait, Koyun.
‎You're not coming to evening practice?

17:17.745 --> 17:19.121
‎He's doing it!

17:19.788 --> 17:24.460
‎No. Most people just tend to talk
‎during the evening practice.

17:24.543 --> 17:27.337
‎I doubt I'd bother anyone
‎if I didn't show up.

17:27.421 --> 17:29.381
‎Okay...

17:29.465 --> 17:31.884
‎Koyuki.
‎That's what evening practice is for.

17:31.967 --> 17:33.844
‎CHEER COUPLES TEND TO EMERGE
‎AFTER THE SPORTS FESTIVAL

17:33.927 --> 17:36.889
‎You could even say it's specific time
‎set aside for people to mingle.

17:36.972 --> 17:39.683
‎-‎This is all implied knowledge.
‎-I've already memorized the moves.

17:39.767 --> 17:42.895
‎-‎This is an overt invitation for you!
‎-Don't worry. I won't let the team down.

17:43.562 --> 17:44.563
‎See you.

17:47.733 --> 17:49.902
‎Keep your chin up, Amamiya.

17:50.486 --> 17:52.404
‎EVENING PRACTICE

17:52.488 --> 17:54.656
‎HERE FOR SOLO PRACTICE

17:54.740 --> 17:56.909
‎HERE TO MINGLE

17:58.368 --> 18:01.080
‎Did I blunder something again?

18:02.664 --> 18:04.083
‎Amamiya!

18:05.375 --> 18:08.587
‎Thank goodness. I'm so relieved.

18:08.670 --> 18:09.671
‎You're relieved?

18:09.755 --> 18:13.675
‎I kind of missed my chance
‎to join a group because I came late.

18:14.343 --> 18:16.553
‎Could we hang out for a bit?

18:20.432 --> 18:24.269
‎Seems like there's cliques popping up
‎all over the place now, huh?

18:24.353 --> 18:26.522
‎Yeah, it happens.

18:27.523 --> 18:30.818
‎It's a shame I won't get the chance
‎to mingle with the seniors

18:30.901 --> 18:32.945
‎once the sports festival is over.

18:33.028 --> 18:35.656
‎You can still speak to us
‎even after the festival?

18:40.202 --> 18:43.831
‎Right! I hung out with Koyun
‎the other day. Just the two of us.

18:43.914 --> 18:44.915
‎You did?

18:44.998 --> 18:46.583
‎When did these two get so close?

18:46.667 --> 18:47.668
‎SLIGHTLY BITTER

18:48.502 --> 18:50.671
‎We had crepes.

18:50.754 --> 18:52.798
‎I've got a few of these.

18:52.881 --> 18:54.174
‎HEH

18:56.635 --> 18:59.930
‎Koyun looks so stiff.

19:02.516 --> 19:06.478
‎Shall I invite you as well
‎the next time Koyun and I hang out?

19:06.562 --> 19:08.438
‎Are you sure you want me there?

19:08.522 --> 19:09.857
‎Of course!

19:09.940 --> 19:12.442
‎I'll make sure to invite you,
‎so please give me your details.

19:12.526 --> 19:13.819
‎Sure.

19:16.613 --> 19:19.449
‎The seniors all get along so well, huh?

19:20.159 --> 19:22.411
‎Koyun's always talking about you guys.

19:22.494 --> 19:25.956
‎About Miki, about Yota...

19:27.416 --> 19:28.458
‎What about me?

19:28.542 --> 19:33.463
‎I'm so jealous of the relationship
‎Koyun and Yota seem to have.

19:34.339 --> 19:35.716
‎What sort of relationship is that?

19:35.799 --> 19:39.595
‎Don't you think those two
‎should just go out already?

19:39.678 --> 19:41.221
‎DOOM

19:41.305 --> 19:42.389
‎SEETHING

19:42.472 --> 19:44.057
‎What makes you say that?

19:44.141 --> 19:46.476
‎Because! Don't they look so good together?

19:47.269 --> 19:51.607
‎Well, we don't know how either of them
‎really feels about each other.

19:52.107 --> 19:54.776
‎Yota probably still likes Miki.

19:54.860 --> 19:57.112
‎And I don't know about Hikawa.

19:57.696 --> 19:59.364
‎Yeah, you're right.

19:59.448 --> 20:02.201
‎-I'm sorry. That was rude of me.
‎-No, not at all.

20:02.284 --> 20:03.619
‎WASN'T TRYING TO REPRIMAND

20:04.203 --> 20:05.245
‎And you're right.

20:05.329 --> 20:07.623
‎Imagine finding out someone
‎who you thought was a friend

20:07.706 --> 20:11.126
‎actually liked you as something more?

20:11.835 --> 20:14.129
‎To think they see you differently...

20:14.713 --> 20:16.882
‎I'd feel a bit disgusted.
‎Wouldn't you agree?

20:16.965 --> 20:18.133
‎CRACK

20:18.217 --> 20:21.637
‎It could even be kind of scary,
‎depending on the situation.

20:23.722 --> 20:25.641
‎-But what's more...
‎-‎There's more?

20:26.225 --> 20:32.397
‎Koyun did say she'd never see her friends
‎as potential love interests.

20:33.148 --> 20:34.149
‎What?

20:40.489 --> 20:41.615
‎You disgust me.

20:48.413 --> 20:51.208
‎Did I cross a line?

22:26.928 --> 22:28.221
‎We made it!

22:37.939 --> 22:39.858
‎Yikes, this is awkward.

22:39.941 --> 22:41.943
‎I know she's on the cheer squad,

22:42.027 --> 22:45.864
‎but it's still super awkward
‎having to deal

22:45.947 --> 22:47.783
‎with the sister of someone
‎I got in a huge fight with.

22:48.492 --> 22:50.452
‎Atagawa. How's your sister?

22:52.120 --> 22:53.705
‎Don't make that face.

22:53.789 --> 22:56.083
‎Aren't you curious
‎about your former classmate?

22:56.625 --> 22:58.168
‎Not really...

23:00.670 --> 23:02.297
‎You really want to know?

23:02.380 --> 23:03.381
‎EEK

23:05.133 --> 23:06.259
‎Wow, it's packed.

23:10.388 --> 23:12.099
‎Sorry about this.

23:12.182 --> 23:15.936
‎No. I'm sorry. For hogging the wall.

23:18.605 --> 23:19.689
‎Koyuki.

23:21.399 --> 23:23.735
‎You're friends with Amamiya, right?

23:24.361 --> 23:27.280
‎What does she mean by that?

23:27.364 --> 23:30.325
‎Yeah, we're friends.

23:31.201 --> 23:35.580
‎The soccer club doesn't allow dating
‎between members and managers.

23:37.874 --> 23:42.295
‎Momoka's been hanging out with you
‎a lot recently, hasn't she?

23:42.963 --> 23:45.298
‎When she used to hang out with me.

23:46.091 --> 23:48.260
‎You do know why, right?

23:50.846 --> 23:54.307
‎Will you please root for her?
